    cards: [
      ["What is Newton's law of cooling?", 'Under suitable conditions, the rate of heat loss is proportional to the temperature difference between an object and its surroundings. The proportionality depends on the object and heat-transfer conditions.'],
      ['What is heat, and what can it do?', 'Energy transferred because of a temperature difference. Heating may raise temperature, cause expansion, change a state of matter or drive physical and chemical changes.'],
      ['What is reflection?', 'The return of a wave into its original medium after meeting a boundary.'],
      ['What are the laws of reflection?', 'The angle of incidence equals the angle of reflection. The incident ray, reflected ray and normal at the point of incidence lie in one plane. Angles are measured from the normal.'],
      ['What is refraction of light?', 'A change in direction as light enters a medium in which its speed differs, except when it enters along the normal.'],
      ['How does a rainbow form?', 'Sunlight is refracted, dispersed into colours and internally reflected inside water droplets. A primary rainbow is seen opposite the Sun. The internal reflection need not be total.'],
      ['What is the focal length of a spherical mirror?', 'The distance from the pole of the mirror to its principal focus.'],
      ['What is the speed of sound in air?', 'About 331 m/s in dry air at 0°C, or 343 m/s at 20°C. It depends on the medium and temperature.'],
      ['What is a transverse wave?', 'A wave whose oscillation is perpendicular to the direction of propagation.'],
      ['What is a longitudinal wave?', 'A wave whose oscillation is parallel to the direction of propagation.'],
      ['What is torque?', 'The turning effect of a force about an axis. Magnitude = force × perpendicular distance from the axis to the line of action. Its SI unit is N·m.'],
      ['What is a capacitor?', 'A device that stores separated electric charge and energy in an electric field.'],
      ['What is weather?', 'The short-term condition of the atmosphere at a place, including temperature, rain, wind and humidity. It is not limited to a fixed one- or two-day period.'],
      ['What is sound?', 'A mechanical disturbance travelling through a medium. Audible sound can produce the sensation of hearing.'],
      ["What is Coulomb's law?", 'The electrostatic force between point charges is proportional to the product of their charges and inversely proportional to the square of their separation: F = k|q₁q₂|/r². Like charges repel; unlike charges attract.'],
    ],
    note: 'Corrects the source on cooling dependence, rainbow reflection, the temperature needed for 331 m/s, and the definition of weather.',
